- `action(n1, "start")`: This action is hallucinated; the source text states "the process begins by filling in their information", which does not imply a separate "start" action.
- `action(n5, "end of process")`: This action is hallucinated; the source text states "the process comes to an end", which corresponds to the `end(e1)` node rather than an action step.
- `actor(a_default, "Default", [...])`: The actor is named "Default", which fails to reflect the "passengers" specified as the actor in the source text.